question/math-academy-id "q-85254" :question/problem "The manager at a water bottle factory notices that, on average, every batch of water bottles has $7$ water bottles on which the label is upside down. What is the probability that the next batch of water bottles will have more than $2$ bottles on which the label is upside down? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that upside-down labels occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
